## Architecture Impact

- architecture_relevance: relevant
- architecture_impact: medium
- architecture_reason: The scope changes an externally consumed protocol error and advertises previously absent client-visible result schemas. It crosses the Core domain contract to MCP adapter/SDK boundary, while retaining current execution, persistence and decision authority.
- architecture_evidence: server.js tool registration and capability-denial branches; run-command-contract.js commandGroupDefinition and budgets; run-command-service.js result construction; mcp-tool-errors.js validateToolDomain; mcp-dispatch-runtime.js failure and decision postprocessing paths.
- architecture_missing_evidence: none for routing. The exact supported pre-handler SDK/transport mechanism and the detailed compact schema layout are explicit later SD decisions, not assumed implementations.
- architecture_next_owner_and_action: prd-definition defines observable contract and compatibility acceptance; sd-definition selects the supported capability-check seam and shared schema/validation ownership before implementation.

## Reuse And Parallel-Structure Risk

| Finding | Evidence | Risk | Required action |
|---|---|---|---|
| problem: model-visible command descriptions and results are incomplete | run-command-contract.js envelope has eleven undescribed properties; commandGroupDefinition omits outputSchema | revise | Existing Core contract owner supplies shared property help and supported result schema; PRD owns behavior and SD owns representation |
| problem: command results have several legitimate shapes | run-command-service.js full envelope, schema-rejection and budget fallback; mcp-dispatch-runtime.js executor failure envelope and decision postprocessing; generation delivery retains producing-runtime descriptors | revise | SD must account for producer, fallback and postprocessed variants through existing owners; do not infer a schema only from one happy-path example |
| problem: high-level SDK handler catches protocol errors | Installed server 2.0.0 dist/mcp-DXXb3Vv3.mjs setToolRequestHandlers catches all handler errors except UrlElicitationRequired; validateToolOutput skips isError; Server._wrapHandler still validates the wire family | revise | SD selects an existing supported pre-execution seam outside that catch; preserve input validation, successful output validation, unknown-tool behavior and version-specific encoding; do not patch node_modules or duplicate an SDK dispatcher |
| problem: declared metadata disagrees with actual contract | plugins/agdf/meta/agdf-mcp-capability.json tool.read_only true versus skill-dispatch/contract.js readOnlyHint false; MCP README current-assembly claim 0.14.5 versus package 0.20.1 | revise | Existing metadata/build owners reconcile and assert consistency; do not introduce a second capability registry |
| problem: adding schemas can exceed existing discovery budgets | RUN_COMMAND_LIMITS definition_bytes 8192 and aggregate_definition_bytes 24576; createMcpDispatchRuntime checks aggregate; decision facade adds its definition to the same budget | revise | SD chooses compact accurate declarations and keeps detail in existing operation-contract help; TP measures ordinary and decision compositions without relaxing limits |
| problem: native contract evidence differs from deterministic conformance | Existing T3 gate approval/T6 stale revision and previous T4 document scenario; historical baseline and existing graph nodes describe distinct environments | warn | TP selects a focused disposable command task, exact host/model/candidate/repetitions and verifier; record failed/unavailable evidence honestly and retain all earlier baselines |

These are known input problems and required downstream decisions, not accepted technical debt. Review pass means ownership and a safe preparation route are understood; it does not resolve the defects or assert implementation readiness. No deliberately retained or newly accepted debt is proposed. A separate diagram is unnecessary: the existing Core command owner -> runtime projection -> SDK adapter boundary is explicit in the cited sources.

## Mode / Slice Decision

- decision: structured_delivery
- required_next_gate: PRD
- scope_reason: external_contract_depth: modern MCP error classification and new advertised command result schemas change a compatibility-sensitive public integration contract. Quick Task and Verified Change are ineligible because this is more than internal correctness and changes external protocol/schema behavior. structured_slice is rejected because full_depth_impacts_absent fails on that evidenced external boundary, not because of file/tool counts.
- evidence: This review's Architecture Impact, Reuse And Parallel-Structure Risk and Structured Depth Evidence; approved UR; packages/mcp-server/src/server.js; packages/core/lib/control-state/run-command-contract.js.
- transparency_note: Full-depth artefacts cover the affected protocol, domain/result, compatibility and evidence boundaries only. No deployment, migration, new permission model or tool regrouping is added. Existing PRD/SD/TP human gates remain necessary.

